  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "identifier": "ssrfr",
  "description": "Protects R applications that fetch URLs an attacker can influence from server-side request forgery. Each redirect hop is parsed once, resolved once, and every resolved address is classified before the connection is pinned to a validated address, so a hostname cannot be rebound between check and connect. Refusals carry stable reason codes. Provides the guarded fetch of each hop of a redirect chain, a helper that follows a whole chain, structural inspection of a URL without network access, and resolved inspection of every address a name resolves to.",
  "name": "ssrfr: Server-Side Request Forgery Guard for Outbound Requests",
